  "summary": "System reconnaissance beacon in index.js exfiltrates host identity via HTTPS",
  "details": "index.js loads the https and os modules at the top level and reads host identity fields — os.hostname(), os.userInfo(), and os.platform() — in a shape consistent with a system-information exfiltration beacon. The file is only two files in the published tarball, so the reconnaissance code path is reached as a side effect of loading the package. The package name uses a scope that resembles a legitimate web-tooling namespace, and the collected fields (hostname, current user, platform) are host identifiers with no benign purpose for a shared UI components library.",
